<title>SPAIN: Spain September C/A surplus 79.30 bln pta - BoS.</title>
<headline>Spain September C/A surplus 79.30 bln pta - BoS.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Spain gave the following figures (in billions of pesetas):</p>
<p> BALANCE OF PAYMENTS		SEPT 96    AUG 96     SEPT 95</p>
<p>  C/A balance			 79.30	   -8.6     127.2</p>
<p>  Trade balance		   -236.40	  -163.5    -226.3</p>
<p>  Services			   252.30	   334.4     227.6</p>
<p>  Net tourism receipts	   282.00	   364.5     256.7</p>
<p>  Other services		   -29.70	   -30.1     -29.1</p>
<p>  Dividend income		  -66.60	  -169.7     -32.5</p>
<p>  Transfers			  130.00	    -9.8     158.5</p>
<p>  CAPITAL ACCOUNT		   33.30	   104.2     na</p>
<p>  FINANCIAL ACCOUNT		-71.90	  -107.9     na</p>
<p>  Spanish investment abroad     93.90	   -91.4	60.2</p>
<p>  Foreign investment Spain   1,234.30	    34.2     413.8</p>
<p>  Spanish loans,dep abroad  -1,078.30	  -416.1  -1,051.1</p>
<p>  Foreign loans, deps in Spain-151.00	   506.3     625.1</p>
<p>  Movement of reserves	  -170.70	  -141.0     -36.6</p>
<p>NOTE: The Bank of Spain said latest figures were provisional. Non-classified element (errors and omissions) in latest capital account figures is negative for 40.8 billion pesetas. The financial account category was introduced in January 1996.</p>
<p>-- Madrid Newsroom, + 341 585 8340</p>
</text>
